---
import { Image, getImage } from 'astro:assets';
import artwork from '../../assets/explainers/sketch-files-light.png';
import darkArtwork from '../../assets/explainers/sketch-files-dark.png';
const dark = await getImage({src:darkArtwork,width:1000,format:'webp'});
---
<figure class="paper-surface filesystem-plate" id="plate-files">
 <span class="plate-number">Illustration</span>
 <h3>Find a file, then change part of its contents</h3>
 <div class="artwork">
  <picture><source media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" srcset={dark.src}/><Image src={artwork} alt="A directory branches into recordings and exports. A recording inside the left folder is enlarged into a strip with two portions marked for change." widths={[600,1000,1536]} sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" format="webp" loading="lazy"/></picture>
  <span class="label root">media/</span>
  <span class="label recordings">recordings/</span>
  <span class="label exports">exports/</span>
  <span class="label file">interview.wav</span>
  <span class="label edited">Two portions edited</span>
 </div>
 <figcaption>Directories organise files by path. A program can open media/recordings/interview.wav, seek to a position, and change part of the recording. The strip shows logical portions of that file, not physical disk blocks.</figcaption>
</figure>
<style>
 .filesystem-plate {margin:2rem 0;padding:1.2rem;scroll-margin-top:1rem;font:.8rem/1.6 var(--font-sans)}
 h3 {font:500 1.35rem/1.3 var(--font-serif);margin:0 0 1rem}
 .artwork{position:relative;container-type:inline-size}.artwork img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}
 .label{position:absolute;transform:translate(-50%,-50%);font:500 clamp(11px,2.7cqw,18px)/1.3 var(--font-serif);color:#49453f;white-space:nowrap;text-align:center}
 .root{left:75%;top:19%}.recordings{left:25%;top:70%}.exports{left:75%;top:70%}.file{left:24%;top:76.5%}.edited{left:50%;top:95%}
 figcaption{border-top:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);padding-top:1rem;margin-top:1rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary);font-size:.75rem}
@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){.label{color:#e3dfd4}}
</style>
